attribution: Traditional Korean folk song (the "Bonjo Arirang" of Gyeonggi), transcribed by Homer Hulbert in 1896; melody and words are anonymous and public domain. Written in 9/8 with the eighth note as the beat (dotted quarter = 3 beats), so the tempo is in eighths (about 50 dotted quarters per minute).
tags: korea, folk, pentatonic, unesco

